<title>THAILAND: Thailand says committed to Japan airport loan.</title>
<headline>Thailand says committed to Japan airport loan.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand said on Wednesday that it was still committed to a 70 billion baht loan negotiated with Japan's Overseas Economic Cooperation Fund (OECF) for its now-suspended second airport project.</p>
<p>However, the loan would only be used when the project was resumed in the future, Finance Minister Amnuay Viravan told reporters. He added that the transport and communications ministry had also been directed to study ways to deal with various contracts already signed with private firms for initial work on the second airport.</p>
</text>
